    "evidence_text": "The provided architecture and ontology are language independent.\n\nAlthough some of the NLP modules are language dependent, they can be built using adequate AI methodologies.\n\nIntroduction\tThe automatic identification, extraction and representation of the information conveyed in texts is a key task nowadays.\n\nbase, allowing posterior inferences and reasoning.\n\nEvents are represented by objects having associated actions, agents, elements, places and time.\n\nWe used Freeling  library to provide the tags.\n\nThis library resorts to a Hidden Markov Model as described by Brants .\n\nThe Freeling library also has dependency parsing models for Portuguese.\n\nWe made 589 tag conversions over 14 different categories.\n\nThese rules can be further seen in the corresponding Github repository .\n\nThe modified training and development datasets are also available on another Github repositorypage  for further research and comparison purposes.\n\nwhich are then tagged as A0, A1, AM-TMP, AM-LOC, respectively.\n\nTo do this, we use Euvovoc\n\nFor a more detailed description of ontologies and knowledge bases, see for instance .\n\nNow, considering\n\nIn this way, the proposed method is able to produce a detailed and well-connected knowledge base.\n\nGraphDB is an enterprise-ready Semantic Graph Database, compliant with W3C Standards.\n\nThis is useful when the RDF data structure\n\nIn fact, we have explored the use of already existing modules and adopted and integrated several of these tools into our pipeline.\n\nWe evaluated several systems like Rembrandt  or LinguaKit:\n\nthe former only has the initial steps of our proposal (until NER) and the later performed worse than our system.\n\nAs a final result, the obtained output is inserted into a specialized ontology.",
